{
  "id": "stage-sampling",
  "term": "stage sampling",
  "definition": "Stage sampling is a survey sampling approach carried out in steps rather than all at once. In the two-stage form described here, researchers first randomly select clusters or groups from the population, then randomly select individual elements from within each chosen cluster.",
